  "tier": "told-once",
  "plain": "In 2011, over the Baltic Sea anomaly, an odd shape that his team found on the seafloor and that he calls a UFO, the treasure hunter Dennis Asberg says their radar showed something about 150 metres from the boat, but when they looked there was nothing. He tells Michels he was on board and names Peter Lindberg as he tells it: \"We are alone here. But should be something 150 m from us. Nothing there.\" He tells it as one of several strange things around that expedition, which taken together would suggest the site was being watched or was itself doing something unusual."
